Answer: Based on the source, Donald Trump tested positive for COVID-19 through a "quick-result test" administered as part of White House protocols. The specific type of test (e.g., PCR or antigen) is not identified in this report, but it documents that "President Donald Trump and first lady Melania Trump have tested positive for the coronavirus."

